---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";

/* Single source of truth for the date. Change it here and the countdown,
   the calendar file and every mention on the page follow. */
const START_UTC = "2026-09-29T21:00:00Z"; // 2:00 PM Arizona (no DST, UTC-7)
const DATE_LONG = "Tuesday, September 29";
const TIME_LOCAL = "2:00 PM Arizona";
---

<Base
  title="Free live session — the flip that sells to an investor"
  description="For flippers with a crew already working: how a co-living conversion changes who buys the finished house. Live with Brian and Gina Kingdeski."
  noindex
  bare
>
  <header class="lp-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="web-grid">
        <figure class="web-video">
          <video
            class="vid"
            controls
            preload="metadata"
            playsinline
            poster="/media/glbm-intro-poster.webp"
            width="864"
            height="864"
          >
            <source src="/media/glbm-intro.mp4" type="video/mp4" />
            Your browser can&#8217;t play this video.
            <a href="/media/glbm-intro.mp4">Download it instead</a>.
          </video>
          <figcaption>Brian and Gina, two minutes on what this is.</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <div>
          <span class="kicker">FREE LIVE SESSION &#183; {DATE_LONG} &#183; {TIME_LOCAL}</span>

          <h1>Same house. Same crew.<br />A different buyer.</h1>

          <p class="lede">
            Brian and Gina Kingdeski have flipped for 26 years and done north of 2,300 deals
            in the Phoenix metro. In one hour they'll show you how a co-living conversion
            changes who buys your finished house &mdash; and why that changes the whole deal.
          </p>

          <div class="web-proof">
            <div><b>2,300+</b><span>deals</span></div>
            <div><b>26</b><span>years</span></div>
            <div><b>450+</b><span>doors built</span></div>
          </div>

          <p class="web-count" id="count">&#160;</p>

          <div class="cta-row">
            <a class="btn" href="#register">Save my seat</a>
            <a class="btn ghost" href="#agenda">What's covered</a>
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="band">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>You already know how to run a rehab. That's not the problem.</h2>
      <div class="split">
        <div>
          <p>
            You're bidding against every other flipper for the same inventory and selling
            into the same retail buyer pool. Rates moved. Margins thinned. Days on market
            stretched. None of that is news to you.
          </p>
          <p>
            The house isn't the problem. The buyer is. A family with a mortgage pays what
            the comps say, and the comps are set by houses that produce nothing.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p>
            An investor buying a co-living property is doing different math. They price what
            the house earns by the room, and a well-built eight or ten bedroom conversion
            earns considerably more than a three-bedroom rental on the same footprint.
          </p>
          <p>
            Almost nothing about how you work changes. What you produce at the end does, and
            so does who writes the cheque.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="agenda">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>What you'll walk away with</h2>
      <p>Four things you can use on your next deal, whether or not you ever work with us.</p>
      <ol class="stages" style="margin-top:1.5rem">
        <li>
          <div>
            <b>How to tell in five minutes whether a house converts</b>
            <span>Layout, egress, bathroom placement, parking. The things that kill a conversion, and how to spot them before you walk it.</span>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <div>
            <b>Underwriting by the room instead of the bedroom</b>
            <span>Where room-level rent data comes from, and how to price a house on what it earns rather than what the block comps at.</span>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <div>
            <b>The build standard buyers actually want</b>
            <span>Eight bedrooms and two bathrooms as a floor, ensuite where the numbers support it, and why bathroom count is an underwriting decision rather than a finish choice.</span>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <div>
            <b>Where the finished house goes</b>
            <span>Who the registered buyers are, what has to be documented for a property to qualify, and how financing works when the appraiser is pricing income instead of comps.</span>
          </div>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>Who should be on this call</h2>
      <div class="fit" style="margin-top:2rem">
        <div class="col">
          <h3>Come if you</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Have completed flips behind you &mdash; ideally ten or more</li>
            <li>Already run a crew, or use the same trades on every job</li>
            <li>Buy and finance your own deals</li>
            <li>Are watching retail margins thin and want a different exit</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="col not">
          <h3>Skip it if you</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Haven't done a renovation yet &mdash; this isn't a starting point</li>
            <li>Are looking for passive income</li>
            <li>Want to wholesale rather than build</li>
            <li>Are hoping for a get-rich pitch. It's an hour on how the work is actually done</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p style="margin-top:1.75rem;opacity:.85">
        We'd rather you skip it than sit through an hour that wasn't meant for you.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="signup" id="register">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="web-grid">
        <div>
          <h2>Save your seat</h2>
          <p class="lede" style="color:inherit;opacity:.9">
            Free, live, about an hour including questions. Three details and you're in.
          </p>

          <h3 style="margin:2rem 0 .9rem">What happens after you register</h3>
          <ul class="plain">
            <li>The join link lands in your inbox within a minute</li>
            <li>A reminder the day before, and one an hour before</li>
            <li>A calendar file so it doesn't get buried</li>
            <li>Can't make the 29th? Register anyway and we'll tell you when the next one runs</li>
          </ul>

          <p class="fine" style="margin-top:1.75rem;opacity:.75">
            Live means live &mdash; Brian and Gina answer questions on the call, and that's the
            part you can't get from a recording.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="card" id="form-card">
          <div class="web-when" id="when">
            <div><span>Date</span><b>{DATE_LONG}</b></div>
            <div><span>Time</span><b>{TIME_LOCAL}</b></div>
            <div><span>Cost</span><b>Free</b></div>
          </div>

          <form id="webinarForm" novalidate>
            <div class="hp" aria-hidden="true">
              <label for="wb-company">Company</label>
              <input id="wb-company" name="company" type="text" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off" />
            </div>

            <div class="field">
              <label for="wb-first">First name</label>
              <input id="wb-first" name="firstName" type="text" autocomplete="given-name" required />
            </div>
            <div class="field">
              <label for="wb-email">Email</label>
              <input id="wb-email" name="email" type="email" autocomplete="email" required />
              <p class="hint">This is where the join link goes.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="field">
              <label for="wb-phone">Mobile</label>
              <input id="wb-phone" name="phone" type="tel" autocomplete="tel" required />
              <p class="hint">For the reminder before we start. Nothing else.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="field">
              <label for="wb-flips">Flips you've completed <span class="opt">optional</span></label>
              <select id="wb-flips" name="flipsCompleted">
                <option value="">Select one</option>
                <option>None yet</option>
                <option>1&#8211;4</option>
                <option>5&#8211;9</option>
                <option>10&#8211;15</option>
                <option>More than 15</option>
              </select>
              <p class="hint">Helps us pitch the session at the right level. Skip it if you'd rather.</p>
            </div>

            <button class="submit" type="submit">Save my seat</button>

            <p class="fine" style="margin-top:.9rem;font-size:.78rem;opacity:.7">
              By registering you agree to receive email and text about this webinar and the
              Green Light Buying Machine. Reply STOP to opt out any time.
            </p>
          </form>

          <div class="web-done" id="done" hidden>
            <h3>You're in.</h3>
            <p>
              The join link is on its way. If it hasn't landed in a few minutes check spam,
              then email <a href="mailto:info@greenlightbuyingmachine.com">info@greenlightbuyingmachine.com</a>.
            </p>
            <p style="margin-bottom:0">
              <button class="btn" id="ics" type="button">Add to my calendar</button>
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="wrap" style="text-align:center">
      <h2 style="max-width:24ch;margin-inline:auto">
        Don't just flip houses. Build something that keeps paying.
      </h2>
      <div class="cta-row" style="justify-content:center">
        <a class="btn" href="#register">Save my seat</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <script is:inline define:vars={{ START_UTC }}>
    (function () {
      var START = new Date(START_UTC);

      /* A date is information. A countdown is pressure. */
      var el = document.getElementById("count");
      function tick() {
        var ms = START - new Date();
        if (ms <= 0) { el.textContent = "The session is underway."; return; }
        var d = Math.floor(ms / 86400000);
        var h = Math.floor((ms % 86400000) / 3600000);
        var m = Math.floor((ms % 3600000) / 60000);
        el.textContent = d > 0
          ? d + (d === 1 ? " day " : " days ") + h + "h " + m + "m to go"
          : h + "h " + m + "m to go";
      }
      tick();
      setInterval(tick, 60000);

      var form = document.getElementById("webinarForm");
      var when = document.getElementById("when");
      var done = document.getElementById("done");
      var btn = form.querySelector("[type=submit]");
      var label = btn.textContent;

      form.addEventListener("submit", function (e) {
        e.preventDefault();
        if (!form.checkValidity()) {
          var bad = form.querySelector(":invalid");
          if (bad) { bad.scrollIntoView({ behavior: "smooth", block: "center" }); bad.focus(); }
          form.reportValidity();
          return;
        }

        var payload = {};
        new FormData(form).forEach(function (v, k) { payload[k] = v; });
        payload.source = "webinar";
        payload.page = window.location.pathname;

        btn.disabled = true;
        btn.textContent = "Saving your seat\u2026";

        fetch("/api/webinar-register", {
          method: "POST",
          headers: { "Content-Type": "application/json" },
          body: JSON.stringify(payload)
        })
          .then(function (r) {
            if (!r.ok) throw new Error(r.status);
            form.hidden = true;
            when.hidden = true;
            done.hidden = false;
            done.scrollIntoView({ behavior: "smooth", block: "center" });
          })
          .catch(function () {
            btn.disabled = false;
            btn.textContent = label;
            var box = form.querySelector(".status") || document.createElement("p");
            box.className = "status err";
            box.textContent =
              "That didn\u2019t save. Email info@greenlightbuyingmachine.com and we\u2019ll add you.";
            form.insertBefore(box, form.firstChild);
          });
      });

      document.getElementById("ics").addEventListener("click", function () {
        function stamp(d) { return d.toISOString().replace(/[-:]/g, "").split(".")[0] + "Z"; }
        var end = new Date(START.getTime() + 3600000);
        var ics = [
          "BEGIN:VCALENDAR", "VERSION:2.0", "PRODID:-//Green Light Buying Machine//EN",
          "BEGIN:VEVENT",
          "UID:" + Date.now() + "@greenlightbuyingmachine.com",
          "DTSTAMP:" + stamp(new Date()),
          "DTSTART:" + stamp(START),
          "DTEND:" + stamp(end),
          "SUMMARY:Green Light Buying Machine - live session",
          "DESCRIPTION:Find, fund and flip co-living properties. The join link was emailed to you.",
          "URL:https://greenlightbuyingmachine.com/webinar",
          "END:VEVENT", "END:VCALENDAR"
        ].join("\r\n");
        var a = document.createElement("a");
        a.href = URL.createObjectURL(new Blob([ics], { type: "text/calendar" }));
        a.download = "green-light-webinar.ics";
        a.click();
        URL.revokeObjectURL(a.href);
      });
    })();
  </script>
</Base>

<style is:global>
  .web-grid { display: grid; gap: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 4rem); grid-template-columns: 1fr; align-items: center; }
  @media (min-width: 62rem) { .web-grid { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 24rem) minmax(0, 1fr); } }
  /* the sign-up block keeps words left, form right */
  .signup .web-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  @media (min-width: 62rem) {
    .signup .web-grid { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 24rem); }
  }

  .web-video { margin: 0; max-width: 24rem; margin-inline: auto; }
  .web-video .vid { width: 100%; height: auto; display: block; background: #000;
    border-radius: 3px; border: 1px solid rgba(232, 231, 224, .14);
    filter: brightness(.9); }
  .web-video figcaption { font-family: var(--plan); font-size: .72rem; opacity: .55;
    margin-top: .7rem; text-align: center; }

  .opt { font-family: var(--plan); font-size: .68rem; text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: .06em; opacity: .55; margin-left: .4rem; font-weight: 400; }

  .web-proof { display: flex; gap: 2.25rem; margin: 1.75rem 0 1.1rem; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .web-proof b { font-family: var(--display); font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.65rem;
    color: var(--green-bright); display: block; line-height: 1; }
  .web-proof span { font-size: .8rem; opacity: .7; }

  .web-count { font-family: var(--plan); font-size: .82rem; letter-spacing: .06em;
    color: var(--green-bright); margin: 0 0 1.5rem; min-height: 1.1em; }

  .web-when { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: .75rem;
    padding-bottom: 1.1rem; margin-bottom: 1.25rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); }
  .web-when span { display: block; font-size: .7rem; text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: .06em; opacity: .6; }
  .web-when b { font-family: var(--display); font-size: .92rem; }

  .signup { background: var(--ink); color: var(--paper); }
  .signup .card { color: var(--ink); }
  .signup .plain li { border-color: rgba(232, 231, 224, .2); }

  .web-done h3 { font-size: 1.4rem; margin-bottom: .6rem; }
</style>
